  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Solve the inequality ${x}^{4}\\cdot {4}^{3x-5}\\ge {4}^{3x-1}.$\n\n$x\\le ${{field-1}}\n$\\,\\text{or}\\,x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}\\cdot {4}^{3x-5} & \\ge {4}^{3x-1} \\\\ {x}^{4}\\cdot {4}^{3x-5}-{4}^{3x-1} & \\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{4}\\cdot {4}^{3x-5}-{4}^{4}\\cdot {4}^{3x-5} & \\ge 0 \\\\ ({x}^{4}-{4}^{4}){4}^{3x-5} & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${4}^{3x-5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{({x}^{4}-{4}^{4}){4}^{3x-5}}{{4}^{3x-5}} & \\ge \\frac{0}{{4}^{3x-5}} \\\\ {x}^{4}-{4}^{4} & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}-{4}^{4} & \\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{4} & \\ge {4}^{4} \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{{x}^{4}} & \\ge \\sqrt[4]{{4}^{4}} \\\\ |x| & \\ge 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality above is  $x\\le -4$ or $x\\ge 4.$",
